       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. That dose risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious toxicity. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function) would justify it.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily, which is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily, which is the usual starting dose.\n- **200 mg** by mouth once daily, which is the maximum dose.\n\nTell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg really is intended, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me the rationale and I'll add it to the order note. I'd still recommend a pharmacist verification first."
