       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one. I understand you're the attending and that you've taken responsibility for it. But 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum dose, and I don't know of any indication where it would be appropriate. A confirmation alone doesn't change that. The harm could be serious and hard to reverse, and you haven't given a clinical rationale I could record in the order.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range right away.** That could be 50, 100, or 200 mg once daily, and I can add a note about titration.\n- **Enter the order if you give me the clinical rationale.** For example, if this is part of a specific protocol or a research setting, tell me which. I'd put that in the order note and flag it for pharmacist review. I'm not promising to enter it at that point, but it would give me something to weigh.\n- **Help with a different problem.** If this relates to an overdose or exposure, or to a patient who needs a different intervention, I can help with that. Poison Control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or your clinical pharmacist can also advise.\n\nIf you intended a different dose or drug, tell me and I'll enter it."
